//@version=6
// IF LINE 1 ABOVE SHOWS ONE SLASH, YOUR PASTE DROPPED A CHARACTER.
// It must read exactly:  //@version=6
// "Script could not be translated from: null" and "the Pine version of this
// script is unspecified" both mean that one slash is missing.
// ===========================================================================
//  SUPERTREND SNIPER 5.1
//
//  The trend chart. One band, one moving average, one signal, one panel.
//  It shares its visual language with LIQUIDITY SNIPER on purpose: the same
//  palette, the same BUY/SELL marks, the same position box, the same panel.
//  Veer runs one at a time and switching between them should feel like
//  changing chart, not changing product.
//
//  =========================================================================
//  READ THIS BEFORE YOU TRUST THE NUMBER IN THE BOX.
//
//  THE SUPERTREND FLIP IS NOT AN ENTRY EDGE. Measured on real M1 bars built
//  from tick data, against a matched random control:
//    E-113  at LITERALLY ZERO transaction cost the flip scores -0.0058R and
//           beats random by +0.0021R = 1.2 control se. That is nothing.
//    E-114  with the DEMA gate on, -0.0108R = -3.1 control se. The gate makes
//           it significantly WORSE THAN RANDOM. On the most trending third of
//           days, the best possible case, the edge is 0.6 se: nothing.
//    E-125  the same indicator used as a TRAIL banked 39.6 points where a
//           fixed give-back banked 11.0, and E-126's out-of-sample result
//           EXCEEDED its in-sample one. SuperTrend is an exit.
//    E-158  through prop-firm rules it fails on CONSISTENCY, every time: its
//           best single day is 42.8%-78.4% of its total profit against caps
//           of 35-40%. That is the arithmetic signature of a trend follower.
//           So the sweep goes on funded accounts and this, if it runs at all,
//           runs on Veer's OWN live account. Its worst equity on that sample
//           was -3.5% on 15m and -6.4% on 1h.
//
//  That is why this chart runs a SECOND BOOK. FLIP & HOLD takes the same
//  entries and holds to the opposite flip with no stop, no trail and no
//  stall. If FLIP & HOLD is beating SYSTEM, your exit machinery is costing
//  you money and the panel will say so to your face.
//
//  THE PANEL WAS FIXED TODAY AND THE OLD NUMBER WAS TOO HIGH. Two defects:
//    1  E-151. The ATR trail was armed from a bar's own HIGH and then that
//       SAME bar's LOW was allowed to hit it - peak, then retrace, inside one
//       bar. A stop derived from a bar's extreme cannot be placed until that
//       bar has closed. This is E-118's bug, reintroduced. It is also exactly
//       what E-158 had to fix in funded.py's SuperTrend builder; nobody came
//       back for the Pine.
//    2  The panel booked GROSS points - no spread, no slippage - while every
//       backtest figure quoted for this system is NET. It flattered itself
//       against its own evidence with no way to see it.
//  Both are fixed below and both made the box read higher than the truth.
//  =========================================================================
//
//  WHAT IS ON THE CHART, complete list:
//     BUY / SELL marks         the gated flip, on confirmed bars only
//     the SuperTrend band      two segments, one per direction
//     the DEMA                 one thin line
//     the live position        box, entry, stop, real breakeven, P&L in money
//     session shading          Asia / London / New York
//     one panel, top right
//  Nothing else. It draws NO candles of its own: the white and light blue are
//  Veer's own chart setting and an indicator fighting him for them is noise.
//
//  SIGNALS NEVER DISAPPEAR. Every one fires only on a CONFIRMED bar and is
//  drawn with plotshape, whose output cannot be deleted or moved afterwards.
//
//  THE CORE, and it is the EA's core:
//     SIGNAL   a SuperTrend(7, 1.2) flip
//     GATE     the DEMA must slope the right way (dema >= dema[2] to buy)
//     STOP     2.0 x ATR(14) from the fill
//     TRAIL    3.0 x ATR(14), armed immediately, ratcheted one way
//     STALL    close a trade that has gone nowhere for 25 bars
//     There is no take profit.
//  Unchanged from 5.0. Veer has not asked for a different strategy.
//
//  RUN IT ON XAUUSD M1, M3 or M5. E-081 governs the clock: 0.01 lots is
//  GBP 0.787 a point and cannot be smaller, so the TIMEFRAME sets the risk,
//  not the account. A GBP 40 account trades M1.
//
//  NEVER FORWARD TESTED. Nothing here has met a real spread, a real fill or
//  a real Sunday gap.
// ===========================================================================
indicator("SUPERTREND SNIPER 5.1", overlay = true, max_labels_count = 500,
     max_lines_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 500, max_bars_back = 1000)

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ inputs --
gS = "1 · SIGNAL  (measured; leave alone unless testing)"
stLen   = input.int(7,     "SuperTrend ATR length", group = gS, minval = 1)
stMult  = input.float(1.2, "SuperTrend multiplier", group = gS, step = 0.1)
useDema = input.bool(true, "DEMA slope gate", group = gS,
     tooltip = "The EA ships with this ON and E-114 measured it at -3.1 control se - significantly WORSE than random. It is left on so the chart matches the EA. Turn it off and watch the panel: the refused-flip count in the full panel is what it costs you.")
demaLen = input.int(0,     "DEMA length (0 = per-clock: 60 on M1, 100 on M3, else 200)",
     group = gS, minval = 0)

gE = "2 · RISK / EXIT"
stopAtr  = input.float(2.0, "Initial stop (ATR)", group = gE, step = 0.5)
useTrail = input.bool(true, "ATR trail", group = gE)
trailAtr = input.float(3.0, "Trail distance (ATR)", group = gE, step = 0.5,
     tooltip = "Wide on purpose. Every tighter trail tested lost, on every market tested.")
useSt    = input.bool(false, "Trail on the SuperTrend band instead", group = gE,
     tooltip = "E-125 measured the band against a fixed give-back on the liquidity system and it won 39.6 points to 11.0, with E-126's out-of-sample result exceeding in-sample. That was measured on M15 zones, NOT on this flip system, so it is a switch to test with the panel rather than a default to trust.")
maxStall = input.int(25,    "Close a stalled trade after N bars", group = gE)
maxHold  = input.int(50,    "Absolute ceiling (bars)", group = gE)
tpR      = input.float(0.0, "Hard take profit (R). 0 = none", group = gE, step = 0.5,
     tooltip = "0 by default: this system has no take profit. E-117 measured a fixed target LOSING where riding and protecting the peak won.")

gK = "3 · COST — the panel was lying without this"
// Every backtest figure quoted for this system is NET of costs. The panel used
// to book entry-to-exit gross, so it flattered itself against its own evidence
// and there was no way to see it. Now every trade pays the round trip, and so
// does the FLIP & HOLD shadow book, so the comparison between them stays fair.
spreadPts = input.float(0.30, "Your spread, in points", group = gK, step = 0.05,
     tooltip = "One point = $1.00 of price. Veer's broker runs about 0.20-0.40 on XAUUSD. Charged once per trade: you buy the ask and sell the bid.")
slipPts   = input.float(0.02, "Slippage per side, in points", group = gK, step = 0.01,
     tooltip = "E-118: on this system the entire measured residual was four ticks of gold and it was gone at five. E-129 broke the older system at 0.10. Charged twice - once in, once out.")

gM = "4 · MONEY"
lots     = input.float(0.01,  "Lots", group = gM, step = 0.01, minval = 0.01)
gbpPoint = input.float(0.787, "Account currency per point at 0.01 lots", group = gM,
     step = 0.001,
     tooltip = "E-081. 0.01 lots on XAUUSD is about GBP 0.787 per point and cannot go lower. This is why the TIMEFRAME sets the risk, not the account size.")
ccy      = input.string("£",  "Currency symbol", group = gM)

gT = "5 · SESSIONS"
showSess = input.bool(true, "Show sessions", group = gT)
tzSess   = input.string("Etc/UTC", "Timezone", group = gT)
sessA    = input.session("0000-0800", "Asia",     group = gT)
sessL    = input.session("0700-1600", "London",   group = gT)
sessN    = input.session("1200-2100", "New York", group = gT)
// There is NO session filter on this chart. E-161/E-162 measured sessions on
// the sweep, not on the flip, and a dial with no measurement behind it is a
// way to lose money with extra steps. The shading is there to read by.

gD = "6 · CHART"
cBuy   = input.color(#00B0FF, "Buy",  group = gD, inline = "c1")
cSell  = input.color(#FF3B5C, "Sell", group = gD, inline = "c1")
showBand = input.bool(true, "SuperTrend band", group = gD, inline = "s1")
showDema = input.bool(true, "DEMA",            group = gD, inline = "s1")
showLive = input.bool(true, "Position box",    group = gD, inline = "s1")
showHist = input.bool(false, "Finished trades", group = gD, inline = "s2",
     tooltip = "OFF by default. On M1 this is a P&L label on every closed trade - thousands of them, capped at the last 500 by TradingView - and it is the single biggest source of clutter here. Switch it on to study the history, not to read the market.")
showPanel = input.bool(true, "Panel", group = gD, inline = "s2")
showRefused = input.bool(false, "Mark refused flips", group = gD, inline = "s2",
     tooltip = "OFF by default because it is chart noise: a flip the DEMA gate turned down is something that did NOT happen. The count is in the full panel under 'gate refused', which is the honest place for it.")
sigStyle = input.string("Word labels", "Signal marks", group = gD,
     options = ["Word labels", "Triangles"],
     tooltip = "Word labels match LIQUIDITY SNIPER. Pick triangles if you are running both scripts on one chart, so the two do not write text on the same candles.")
labOff   = input.int(0, "Push this chart's labels right by N bars", group = gD,
     tooltip = "0 keeps the labels where LIQUIDITY SNIPER puts them. Raise it only if you are running both at once and their right-edge text overlaps.")
panelPos = input.string("Top right", "Panel position", group = gD,
     options = ["Top right", "Bottom right", "Bottom left"],
     tooltip = "TOP RIGHT on purpose - Veer asked for a small profit box up there, and LIQUIDITY SNIPER's panel sits bottom right, so the two never collide.")
panelBig = input.bool(false, "Show the full panel", group = gD,
     tooltip = "Off: the profit box - points, trades, win rate, the exit comparison and the live trade. On: adds how trades ended, the risk block and the session row.")

// ----------------------------------------------------------------- helpers --
f_num(x, d) =>
    (x >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(x, d)
f_ccy(v) =>
    (v >= 0 ? "+" : "-") + ccy + str.tostring(math.abs(v) * gbpPoint * lots / 0.01, "0.00")

// The round trip, charged once per closed trade: the spread once (you buy the
// ask and sell the bid) and slippage twice (in and out).
cost = spreadPts + 2.0 * slipPts

// ------------------------------------------------------------------- maths --
atr = ta.atr(14)
[stLine, stDir] = ta.supertrend(stMult, stLen)
bull = stDir == -1

// The EA's per-clock DEMA rule. Pine has no ta.dema, so it is built from two
// EMAs exactly as the EA builds it. Pine's ta.ema is SMA-seeded, which is what
// the EA was changed to in 2.30 - that seeding difference was a real source of
// signal drift before P92.
dLen = demaLen > 0 ? demaLen :
       timeframe.period == "1" ? 60 :
       timeframe.period == "3" ? 100 : 200
e1   = ta.ema(close, dLen)
dema = 2 * e1 - ta.ema(e1, dLen)

flipUp   = bull and not bull[1]
flipDown = not bull and bull[1]
gateBuy  = not useDema or dema >= dema[2]
gateSell = not useDema or dema <= dema[2]

buySig  = flipUp   and gateBuy  and barstate.isconfirmed
sellSig = flipDown and gateSell and barstate.isconfirmed
refuseB = flipUp   and not gateBuy  and barstate.isconfirmed
refuseS = flipDown and not gateSell and barstate.isconfirmed

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- sessions --
// Detection is kept separate from drawing so that hiding the shading can never
// silently change anything else. Nothing here gates a trade on this chart.
inASess = not na(time(timeframe.period, sessA, tzSess))
inLSess = not na(time(timeframe.period, sessL, tzSess))
inNSess = not na(time(timeframe.period, sessN, tzSess))
inA = showSess and inASess
inL = showSess and inLSess
inN = showSess and inNSess
bgcolor(inN ? color.new(#F5A623, 95) : inL ? color.new(#4A90D9, 96) :
     inA ? color.new(#7B68EE, 97) : na, title = "Sessions")

// -------------------------------------------------------- position state ----
// Pine has no comma-separated declarations - one name per line.
var int   posDir   = 0
var float posEntry = na
var float posStop  = na
var float posInit  = na
var float posTp    = na
var float posPeak  = na
var int   posBar   = na
var int   stallBar = na

// the shadow book: the SAME entries, no exit machinery at all
var int   shDir   = 0
var float shEntry = na
var int   shN     = 0
var float shPts   = 0.0

// ------------------------------------------------------------ book-keeping --
var int   nTrades = 0
var int   nWins   = 0
var float sumPts  = 0.0
var float bestPts = 0.0
var float worstPts= 0.0
var float peakEq  = 0.0
var float maxDD   = 0.0
var int   nLong   = 0
var int   nShort  = 0
var float ptsLong = 0.0
var float ptsShort= 0.0
var int   nStop   = 0
var int   nTrail  = 0
var int   nStall  = 0
var int   nAged   = 0
var int   nFlip   = 0
var int   nTp     = 0
var int   nGate   = 0
var int   firstT  = 0

if refuseB or refuseS
    nGate += 1

// ==================== THE LIVE POSITION, DRAWN =============================
// ONE set of objects, created on the fill, moved each bar, deleted on the exit.
// Creating a fresh set per bar is what fills the 500-object budget in an
// afternoon and makes the chart stutter.
var box   pBox   = na
var line  pEntry = na
var line  pStop  = na
var line  pBe    = na
var line  pTp    = na
var label lStop  = na
var label lBe    = na
var label lTp    = na
var label lLive  = na

// Pine takes a function's last expression as its return value, and a body made
// only of if-statements returns na. Returning an explicit bool keeps the type
// unambiguous wherever it is called.
f_killLive() =>
    if not na(pBox)
        box.delete(pBox)
    if not na(pEntry)
        line.delete(pEntry)
    if not na(pStop)
        line.delete(pStop)
    if not na(pBe)
        line.delete(pBe)
    if not na(pTp)
        line.delete(pTp)
    if not na(lStop)
        label.delete(lStop)
    if not na(lBe)
        label.delete(lBe)
    if not na(lTp)
        label.delete(lTp)
    if not na(lLive)
        label.delete(lLive)
    true

// ============================ THE SHADOW BOOK ==============================
// Flip in, opposite flip out. No stop, no trail, no stall, no target. It pays
// the SAME round trip as the real book, because a comparison between a costed
// book and a free one answers nothing.
//
// It takes exactly the same entries: flips alternate, so at every buy signal
// the shadow is either flat or short, and a short is closed by that same flip
// on the line above. The panel prints both trade counts so you can see that.
if shDir != 0 and barstate.isconfirmed and ((shDir > 0 and flipDown) or (shDir < 0 and flipUp))
    shPts += shDir * (close - shEntry) - cost
    shN   += 1
    shDir := 0
if (buySig or sellSig) and shDir == 0
    shDir   := buySig ? 1 : -1
    shEntry := close

// ============================== THE REAL BOOK ==============================
// The exit is evaluated BEFORE the entry so that one flip can close a trade
// and open the opposite one on the same bar.
//
// E-110: nothing is checked on the entry bar. That is correct HERE and it is
// not a contradiction of LIQUIDITY SNIPER, which does allow its stop on the
// entry bar: this system enters at the CLOSE of a confirmed flip bar, so that
// bar is already over and there is no intra-bar risk left in it. LIQUIDITY
// SNIPER enters intra-bar on a resting order, so the rest of its entry bar is
// live and a move running straight through it is a real loss.
var float exitPx = na
var string exitWhy = ""
closedNow = false

if posDir != 0 and barstate.isconfirmed and bar_index > posBar
    // ---- 1. THE STOP THAT WAS ALREADY RESTING IS TESTED FIRST. -------------
    // This ordering is the E-151 / E-118 fix and it is not cosmetic. The old
    // code moved the trail up using THIS bar's high and then let THIS bar's
    // low hit the level it had just invented - peak, then retrace, inside one
    // minute, at a price no order was ever sitting at.
    hitStop = posDir > 0 ? low <= posStop : high >= posStop
    hitTp   = not na(posTp) and (posDir > 0 ? high >= posTp : low <= posTp)
    aged    = bar_index - posBar >= maxHold
    flipOut = (posDir > 0 and flipDown) or (posDir < 0 and flipUp)

    // ---- 2. only if it survived does this bar's extreme move the trail -----
    trailOut = false
    if not hitStop
        if posDir > 0 ? high > posPeak : low < posPeak
            posPeak  := posDir > 0 ? high : low
            stallBar := bar_index
        if useTrail
            cand = useSt ? stLine :
                 posDir > 0 ? posPeak - trailAtr * atr : posPeak + trailAtr * atr
            if posDir > 0 ? cand > posStop : cand < posStop
                // THE E-151 CLAMP. The new level comes from this bar, so it
                // cannot be placed until this bar has closed - and if price
                // has already gone past it, no order could be resting there.
                // A sell-stop ABOVE the market does not exist. The reference
                // implementation (engine.trail_level) calls that EXIT NOW, at
                // this bar's close, and so does this.
                if posDir > 0 ? cand >= close : cand <= close
                    trailOut := true
                else
                    posStop := cand

    stalled = bar_index - stallBar >= maxStall

    // a bar that touches both the stop and the target is scored as the LOSS
    if hitStop or hitTp or stalled or aged or flipOut or trailOut
        // A stop does not fill at its price when the bar OPENS past it - it
        // fills at the open, which is worse. On M1 that is about 15% of exits
        // and booking the stop price for them flatters the book.
        gapPx   = posDir > 0 ? (open <= posStop ? open : posStop) :
                 (open >= posStop ? open : posStop)
        // The take profit is a LIMIT order: it fills at its price or better,
        // so booking the level is the conservative side of that trade.
        exitPx  := hitStop ? gapPx : hitTp ? posTp : close
        exitWhy := hitStop ? (posStop == posInit ? "stop" : "trail") :
                 hitTp ? "tp" : trailOut ? "trail" : flipOut ? "flip" :
                 stalled ? "stall" : "time"
        // NET, not gross.
        pts = posDir * (exitPx - posEntry) - cost
        if nTrades == 0
            firstT := time
        nTrades  += 1
        nWins    += pts > 0 ? 1 : 0
        sumPts   += pts
        bestPts  := math.max(bestPts,  pts)
        worstPts := math.min(worstPts, pts)
        peakEq   := math.max(peakEq, sumPts)
        maxDD    := math.max(maxDD, peakEq - sumPts)
        if posDir > 0
            nLong   += 1
            ptsLong += pts
        else
            nShort   += 1
            ptsShort += pts
        if exitWhy == "stop"
            nStop += 1
        else if exitWhy == "trail"
            nTrail += 1
        else if exitWhy == "stall"
            nStall += 1
        else if exitWhy == "flip"
            nFlip += 1
        else if exitWhy == "tp"
            nTp += 1
        else
            nAged += 1
        if showHist
            label.new(bar_index, posDir > 0 ? math.max(posEntry, exitPx) : math.min(posEntry, exitPx),
                 f_num(pts, "0.0") + "pt " + f_ccy(pts),
                 style = posDir > 0 ? label.style_label_lower_left : label.style_label_upper_left,
                 color = color.new(chart.bg_color, 100),
                 textcolor = color.new(pts > 0 ? cBuy : cSell, 15), size = size.tiny)
        posDir   := 0
        posEntry := na
        posStop  := na
        posTp    := na
        posBar   := na
        closedNow := true

// ---- the objects go with the trade, and BEFORE any re-entry ---------------
// This block has to sit between the exit and the entry: if it ran afterwards,
// a flip that closed one trade and opened the next would leave the first
// trade's box and lines on the chart forever.
if (posDir == 0 or not showLive) and not na(pEntry)
    f_killLive()
    pBox   := na
    pEntry := na
    pStop  := na
    pBe    := na
    pTp    := na
    lStop  := na
    lBe    := na
    lTp    := na
    lLive  := na

// ------------------------------------------------------------- the entry ---
// The fill is the CLOSE of the confirmed flip bar - a market order, which is a
// price you can actually get. There is no f_fill here because nothing is
// resting at a level: E-165 killed the sweep's entry precisely because it
// booked a level the market had already left, and this system never books one.
takeBuy  = posDir == 0 and buySig
takeSell = posDir == 0 and sellSig

if takeBuy or takeSell
    posDir   := takeBuy ? 1 : -1
    posEntry := close
    posStop  := takeBuy ? close - stopAtr * atr : close + stopAtr * atr
    posInit  := posStop
    posTp    := tpR > 0 ? posEntry + posDir * tpR * math.abs(posEntry - posInit) : na
    posBar   := bar_index
    posPeak  := close
    stallBar := bar_index

if (takeBuy or takeSell) and showLive and posDir != 0
    f_killLive()
    col = posDir > 0 ? cBuy : cSell
    pBox := box.new(posBar, posEntry, bar_index, close,
         border_color = color.new(col, 60), border_width = 1,
         bgcolor = color.new(col, 93))
    pEntry := line.new(posBar, posEntry, bar_index, posEntry,
         color = color.new(#B0BEC5, 20), width = 1)
    pStop := line.new(posBar, posStop, bar_index, posStop,
         color = color.new(cSell, 15), width = 1, style = line.style_dashed)
    lStop := label.new(bar_index + labOff, posStop, "", style = label.style_label_left,
         color = color.new(chart.bg_color, 100), textcolor = color.new(cSell, 0),
         size = size.tiny)
    lLive := label.new(bar_index + labOff, close, "", style = label.style_label_left,
         color = color.new(chart.bg_color, 100), textcolor = color.new(col, 0),
         size = size.small)
    // THE REAL BREAKEVEN. Not the entry - the price at which the trade nets
    // zero after the spread and both sides of slippage. Until the stop is past
    // this line, "it's at breakeven" is a story.
    bePx = posEntry + posDir * cost
    pBe := line.new(posBar, bePx, bar_index, bePx,
         color = color.new(#8FA3B8, 40), width = 1, style = line.style_dotted)
    lBe := label.new(bar_index + labOff, bePx, "", style = label.style_label_left,
         color = color.new(chart.bg_color, 100), textcolor = color.new(#8FA3B8, 10),
         size = size.tiny)
    if not na(posTp)
        pTp := line.new(posBar, posTp, bar_index, posTp,
             color = color.new(cBuy, 30), width = 1, style = line.style_dotted)
        lTp := label.new(bar_index + labOff, posTp, "", style = label.style_label_left,
             color = color.new(chart.bg_color, 100), textcolor = color.new(cBuy, 10),
             size = size.tiny)

// ---- move the live objects. Once per bar, never recreated. -----------------
if posDir != 0 and showLive and not na(pEntry)
    live = posDir * (close - posEntry) - cost
    col  = live >= 0 ? cBuy : cSell
    box.set_right(pBox, bar_index)
    box.set_top(pBox, math.max(posEntry, close))
    box.set_bottom(pBox, math.min(posEntry, close))
    box.set_bgcolor(pBox, color.new(col, 93))
    box.set_border_color(pBox, color.new(col, 60))
    line.set_x2(pEntry, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(pStop, bar_index)
    line.set_y1(pStop, posStop)
    line.set_y2(pStop, posStop)
    // NET. A stop at the entry price is not breakeven - you are still down the
    // round trip. This is the number that says whether the trade is safe yet.
    locked = posDir * (posStop - posEntry) - cost
    label.set_xy(lStop, bar_index + labOff, posStop)
    label.set_text(lStop, (locked >= 0 ? "LOCKED " : "SL ") + f_num(locked, "0.0")
         + "pt " + f_ccy(locked))
    label.set_textcolor(lStop, color.new(locked >= 0 ? cBuy : cSell, 0))
    label.set_xy(lLive, bar_index + labOff, close)
    // posDir, NOT bull: on a forming bar the band can flip before the exit
    // block gets to run (it only runs on a confirmed bar), and a label that
    // reads LONG over a short position is worse than no label.
    label.set_text(lLive, (posDir > 0 ? "LONG " : "SHORT ") + f_num(live, "0.0")
         + "pt " + f_ccy(live))
    label.set_textcolor(lLive, color.new(col, 0))
    if not na(pBe)
        bePx2 = posEntry + posDir * cost
        line.set_x2(pBe, bar_index)
        line.set_y1(pBe, bePx2)
        line.set_y2(pBe, bePx2)
        label.set_xy(lBe, bar_index + labOff, bePx2)
        // it turns buy-coloured once the stop is past it: from that point the
        // trade genuinely cannot lose money
        safe = posDir * (posStop - bePx2) >= 0
        label.set_text(lBe, safe ? "BREAKEVEN · locked in" : "BREAKEVEN")
        label.set_textcolor(lBe, color.new(safe ? cBuy : #8FA3B8, 10))
    if not na(pTp)
        line.set_x2(pTp, bar_index)
        label.set_xy(lTp, bar_index + labOff, posTp)
        label.set_text(lTp, "TP " + f_num(posDir * (posTp - posEntry) - cost, "0.0")
             + "pt " + f_ccy(posDir * (posTp - posEntry) - cost))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- drawing --
// The band is drawn as TWO series, one per direction, so it breaks at a flip
// instead of drawing a vertical line straight through the candles.
stUp = showBand and bull ? stLine : na
stDn = showBand and not bull ? stLine : na
plot(stUp, "SuperTrend up",   color = color.new(cBuy, 30),  linewidth = 2,
     style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(stDn, "SuperTrend down", color = color.new(cSell, 30), linewidth = 2,
     style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(showDema ? dema : na, "DEMA", color = color.new(#8FA3B8, 55), linewidth = 1)

// SIGNALS ARE plotshape ON CONFIRMED BARS. plotshape output cannot be deleted
// or moved after the fact, so these can never vanish from history.
wordSig = sigStyle == "Word labels"
plotshape(takeBuy and wordSig, "BUY", shape.labelup, location.belowbar,
     color = cBuy,  text = "BUY",  textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(takeSell and wordSig, "SELL", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar,
     color = cSell, text = "SELL", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(takeBuy and not wordSig, "BUY (triangle)", shape.triangleup,
     location.belowbar, color = cBuy,  size = size.small)
plotshape(takeSell and not wordSig, "SELL (triangle)", shape.triangledown,
     location.abovebar, color = cSell, size = size.small)
// a flip the DEMA gate refused. Off by default: it is something that did NOT
// happen, and the count belongs in the panel rather than on the candles.
plotshape(showRefused and refuseB, "gate refused (buy)", shape.circle,
     location.belowbar, color = color.new(cBuy, 70),  size = size.tiny)
plotshape(showRefused and refuseS, "gate refused (sell)", shape.circle,
     location.abovebar, color = color.new(cSell, 70), size = size.tiny)

// ================================ THE PANEL ================================
var table tp = na

f_row(r, a, b, c, col) =>
    table.cell(tp, 0, r, a, text_color = color.new(#8FA3B8, 0), text_size = size.small,
         text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(tp, 1, r, b, text_color = col, text_size = size.small,
         text_halign = text.align_right)
    table.cell(tp, 2, r, c, text_color = color.new(#8FA3B8, 25), text_size = size.tiny,
         text_halign = text.align_right)

f_sep(r, cap) =>
    table.cell(tp, 0, r, cap, text_color = color.new(#5C7089, 0), text_size = size.tiny,
         text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(tp, 1, r, "", text_color = color.new(#5C7089, 0))
    table.cell(tp, 2, r, "", text_color = color.new(#5C7089, 0))

if barstate.islast and showPanel
    if not na(tp)
        table.delete(tp)
    pos = panelPos == "Top right" ? position.top_right :
          panelPos == "Bottom left" ? position.bottom_left : position.bottom_right
    // The panel is exactly as tall as the rows it will actually draw. A
    // hard-coded row count silently drops the last rows the day a block is
    // added, and that is what the 5.0 panel did.
    // title + measured over + if traded + trades + win rate + avg trade   6
    // separator + SYSTEM + FLIP & HOLD + exit adds                          4
    // cost paid + open                                                      2
    // the footer separator                                                  1
    // the full block: 2 separators, 3 endings, 4 risk, gate, session        11
    nRows = 6 + 4 + 2 + 1 + (panelBig ? 11 : 0)
    tp := table.new(pos, 3, nRows, border_width = 1,
         bgcolor = color.new(#0E1621, 8), border_color = color.new(#2A3A4D, 40),
         frame_color = color.new(#2A3A4D, 20), frame_width = 1)

    cVal  = color.new(#E6EDF5, 0)
    cPos  = color.new(cBuy, 0)
    cNeg  = color.new(cSell, 0)
    winPc = nTrades > 0 ? 100.0 * nWins / nTrades : 0.0
    avg   = nTrades > 0 ? sumPts / nTrades : 0.0
    days  = nTrades > 0 ? math.max(1.0, (time - firstT) / 86400000.0) : 1.0

    table.cell(tp, 0, 0, "SUPERTREND SNIPER", text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small,
         text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(tp, 1, 0, "", text_color = cVal)
    table.cell(tp, 2, 0, posDir == 0 ? (bull ? "bull · flat" : "bear · flat") :
         posDir > 0 ? "LONG" : "SHORT",
         text_color = posDir == 0 ? color.new(#8FA3B8, 0) : posDir > 0 ? cPos : cNeg,
         text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_right)

    // Rows are placed from a running counter, not from hard-coded indices, so
    // hiding a block cannot leave a hole or stack two rows on each other.
    row = 1

    // WHAT PERIOD IS THIS? It is every bar TradingView has loaded on the
    // chart - roughly a fortnight on M1, not today - so the range is printed.
    f_row(row, "measured over",
             nTrades > 0 ? str.format("{0,date,dd MMM}", firstT) : "-",
             "to " + str.format("{0,date,dd MMM}", time), cVal)
    row += 1
    // POINTS FIRST (E-074: expectancy is not money), and NET, and labelled
    // "if traded" rather than "profit" because that is what it is: what these
    // signals would have paid on the bars loaded. It is a measurement of a
    // sample, never a promise, and E-113/E-114 say what to expect of it.
    f_row(row, "if traded", f_num(sumPts, "0.0") + "pt", f_ccy(sumPts),
             sumPts >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg)
    row += 1
    f_row(row, "trades", str.tostring(nTrades),
             str.tostring(nTrades / days, "0.0") + "/day", cVal)
    row += 1
    f_row(row, "win rate", str.tostring(winPc, "0.0") + "%",
             str.tostring(nWins) + "W " + str.tostring(nTrades - nWins) + "L", cVal)
    row += 1
    f_row(row, "avg trade", f_num(avg, "0.000") + "pt", f_ccy(avg),
             avg >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg)
    row += 1

    // ---- is the exit machinery earning its keep? --------------------------
    // Both books pay the same round trip on the same number of trades, so the
    // COST CANCELS in "exit adds" and that row is a clean comparison of the
    // exit rules alone.
    f_sep(row, "── is the exit paying? ──")
    row += 1
    f_row(row, "SYSTEM", f_num(sumPts, "0.0") + "pt",
             "stop/trail/stall · " + str.tostring(nTrades), sumPts >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg)
    row += 1
    f_row(row, "FLIP & HOLD", f_num(shPts, "0.0") + "pt",
             "flip to flip · " + str.tostring(shN), shPts >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg)
    row += 1
    f_row(row, "exit adds", f_num(sumPts - shPts, "0.0") + "pt",
             f_ccy(sumPts - shPts), sumPts - shPts >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg)
    row += 1

    // THE COST PAID, in full. Every trade pays the round trip again, so a
    // system that trades 147 times a day pays it 147 times a day.
    costPaid = nTrades * cost
    f_row(row, "cost paid", "-" + str.tostring(costPaid, "0.0") + "pt",
             f_ccy(-costPaid), cNeg)
    row += 1
    f_row(row, "open", posDir == 0 ? "-" : f_num(posDir * (close - posEntry) - cost, "0.0") + "pt",
             posDir == 0 ? str.tostring(lots, "0.00") + " lots"
                         : f_ccy(posDir * (close - posEntry) - cost),
             posDir == 0 ? cVal :
                 (posDir * (close - posEntry) - cost >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg))
    row += 1
    f_sep(row, "the flip is an EXIT, not an entry · E-114 / E-125")
    row += 1

    if panelBig
        f_sep(row, "── how trades ended ──")
        row += 1
        f_row(row, "stop / trail", str.tostring(nStop) + " / " + str.tostring(nTrail),
                 "", cVal)
        row += 1
        f_row(row, "stall / flip", str.tostring(nStall) + " / " + str.tostring(nFlip),
                 "", cVal)
        row += 1
        f_row(row, "time / target", str.tostring(nAged) + " / " + str.tostring(nTp),
                 "", cVal)
        row += 1
        f_sep(row, "── risk ──")
        row += 1
        f_row(row, "worst trade", f_num(worstPts, "0.0") + "pt", f_ccy(worstPts), cNeg)
        row += 1
        f_row(row, "best trade", f_num(bestPts, "0.0") + "pt", f_ccy(bestPts), cPos)
        row += 1
        f_row(row, "max drawdown", f_num(-maxDD, "0.0") + "pt", f_ccy(-maxDD), cNeg)
        row += 1
        // CLAUDE.md requires a long/short split on every claim.
        f_row(row, "long / short",
                 f_num(ptsLong, "0.0") + " / " + f_num(ptsShort, "0.0") + "pt",
                 str.tostring(nLong) + "L " + str.tostring(nShort) + "S",
                 ptsLong >= 0 and ptsShort >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg)
        row += 1
        // what the gate costs, counted rather than argued about (E-114)
        f_row(row, "gate refused", str.tostring(nGate),
                 useDema ? "flips declined" : "gate off", cVal)
        row += 1
        f_row(row, "session",
                 inN ? "New York" : inL ? "London" : inA ? "Asia" : "closed",
                 str.tostring(atr, "0.00") + " ATR", cVal)

plot(posDir, "Position (1 long, -1 short)", display = display.status_line)
plot(posDir != 0 ? posEntry : na, "Entry", display = display.status_line)
plot(posDir != 0 ? posDir * (close - posEntry) - cost : na, "Open points (net)",
     display = display.status_line)
plot(bull ? 1 : -1, "SuperTrend (1 bull)", display = display.status_line)
plot(dema, "DEMA", display = display.status_line)
plot(atr,  "ATR(14)", display = display.status_line)

alertcondition(takeBuy,   "ST BUY",   "SuperTrend Sniper BUY")
alertcondition(takeSell,  "ST SELL",  "SuperTrend Sniper SELL")
alertcondition(closedNow, "ST CLOSE", "SuperTrend Sniper trade closed")
